<title>FRANCE: Metaleurop sees strong zinc outlook.</title>
<headline>Metaleurop sees strong zinc outlook.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Non-ferrous metal producer Metaleurop said on Wednesday that fundamentals pointed to a positive outlook for zinc prices in 1997.</p>
<p>But the group was more cautious on prospects for lead, forecasting prices would remain around an average level $700 per tonne.</p>
<p>&quot;We are more optimistic on zinc as we are now entering a structural shortfall phase. Demand for zinc is strong and we are expecting LME destocking of some 200,000 tonnes this year. We are rather positive on the price outlook,&quot; board member Christian Bue told a group of reporters.</p>
</text>
